d to carry retained declaration/provenance; do not mutate shared historical destinationRules4, application-install-v2 or existing cohort rows. Update native catalogue, generated text/pins and complete goldens only for new identities; old journal replay must remain byte/semantic-identical.\n5. For OLD Destination host compatibility: enforce a live host-side path/declaration check at file judge AND immediately before write/mint-side effects. No declaration proof =\u003e fail closed. Existing file-judge schema accepts only confirmed {head,present,tree}; its present:false produces recorded aborted publication reason path-invalid, NOT a new reserved-path reason. A new refusal schema cannot be returned to old rules without refusal/unknown. Preserve exact old evidence and use present:false as deterministic recorded refusal; document legacy reason granularity. Do not return null as deliberate denial (that means uncertainty).\n6. Legacy missing declarations default-deny publication. If hosted existing Lending must keep publishing before next releases/rooms, explicit reviewed migration authority is needed: finite exact signed-release/definition pin -\u003e shelf/ compatibility mapping, never a name-based exception or global shelf default. This is a policy choice requiring planner approval; no such mapping is implemented.\n\nImplementation slices: pure bounded publication-path/prefix policy; new package reader/build schema and package tests; new native install/provenance + Destination/cohort versions; old-host live compatibility fence and recorded outcome tests; next Grow/Lending package releases; docs/application-views/package docs and fold-publication section6 supersession; D1 owner/seal updates after actual authored source. Existing approved releases/pins untouched.\n\nRequired witnesses: reserved GitHub/instruction/control-extent paths; case and symlink aliases; reserved/overlapping install prefix; missing/unknown declaration; allowed shelf path; stale changed rules; old-host recorded aborted refusal; no mint/push on deny; exact new native reason; old journal replay; Lending shelf positive; Grow no-publication install. Original budgets/deadlines remain. Source inspection establishes no runtime or deploy acceptance.\n\nDecisions needed before implementation: (a) legacy Lending deny-until-upgrade versus reviewed exact-pin compatibility mapping; (b) accept old recorded path-invalid refusal granularity or authorize separate versioned outcome work; (c) approve signed semantic format version/new cohort sequencing. Prefix overlap must include added rules patterns and effective symlink paths; blanket intersection with the catch-all source extent would wrongly deny every file, so reserve the rules/authority extent rather than all ordinary content extents.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true"}}